(footprint "USB_C_Receptacle_HongCheng_HC-TYPE-C-16P_MidMount"
	(version 20260206)
	(generator "pcbnew")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Hong Cheng HC-TYPE-C-16P-C16B (LCSC C19274022), mid-mount (sinking) USB-C 16P, USB 2.0. Body sinks 1.60 mm below the board top, so it is flush with the bottom of a 1.6 mm PCB. Needs a 9.24 x 5.75 mm cutout opening onto the board edge, shown here on F.Fab: it belongs to the board outline (ergogen _port_slots), because a notch drawn on a footprint's Edge.Cuts only T-joins the edge and KiCad rejects that as a malformed outline. Land pattern measured off the manufacturer drawing, https://www.lcsc.com/product-detail/C19274022.html . The C10B (C19274021) and C08B (C19274020) sink 1.00 and 0.80 mm and share this footprint exactly. Do not import the EasyEDA model for this part: it places the shell holes 11.25 mm apart instead of 10.79 and cuts the slot 6.40 deep instead of 5.75.")
	(tags "usb usb-c 2.0 mid-mount sinking")
